# The security CI stage reads this file and passes each id to pip-audit as
# --ignore-vuln. Every entry needs a reason and a review date; an entry with no
# fix available is a tracked risk, not a resolved one.
#
# Format: one advisory id per line. Comments and blank lines are ignored.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PYSEC-2026-1325 - ecdsa 0.19.2
#
# Reached transitively: python-jose[cryptography] -> ecdsa (confirmed with
# `pip show ecdsa` -> Required-by: python-jose).
#
# NO FIX VERSION EXISTS. pip-audit reports an empty "Fix Versions" column, so
# there is no upgrade that clears it and failing the build on it would block
# every pull request indefinitely.
#
# Exposure assessment: the advisory concerns side-channel resistance in ecdsa's
# pure-Python implementation. This application signs JWTs with HS256
# (settings.ALGORITHM = "HS256"), which is HMAC-SHA256 and does not use ECDSA at
# all. The vulnerable code path is not reachable from how python-jose is used
# here. It would become reachable if ALGORITHM were changed to ES256/ES384/ES512.
#
# REMEDIATION (recommended, not yet done): replace python-jose with PyJWT.
# python-jose is minimally maintained and drags in ecdsa and rsa; PyJWT uses
# `cryptography` directly and would drop this dependency entirely. Tracked in
# docs/CICD.md "Accepted security findings".
PYSEC-2026-1325
